WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.103
You have a carefully built Boolean search.

00:00:03.265 --> 00:00:06.144
An AI suggests one more alternative word.

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:08.451
Is this just a small change to how results

00:00:08.471 --> 00:00:10.333
are scored? Or could it change which

00:00:10.353 --> 00:00:12.511
records are allowed into the results at

00:00:12.531 --> 00:00:14.250
all? Make a prediction.

00:00:16.654 --> 00:00:19.334
In a formal Boolean strategy, an OR

00:00:19.354 --> 00:00:21.847
alternative can open another route into

00:00:21.867 --> 00:00:23.096
the eligible set.

00:00:23.271 --> 00:00:26.099
The new word does not merely receive a low

00:00:26.119 --> 00:00:28.573
weight. It changes an admission rule.

00:00:29.476 --> 00:00:32.167
Use the chapter's four tiny records.

00:00:32.342 --> 00:00:35.234
D one and D four contain delulu.

00:00:35.396 --> 00:00:38.056
All four contain job after lowercasing.

00:00:38.283 --> 00:00:41.510
For delulu AND job, a record must satisfy

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:42.927
both conditions.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:45.015
D one and D four pass.

00:00:45.577 --> 00:00:48.355
This is an intersection: keep identifiers

00:00:48.375 --> 00:00:49.784
shared by the sets.

00:00:49.947 --> 00:00:53.754
D two and D three satisfy job but fail the

00:00:53.774 --> 00:00:54.978
delulu condition.

00:00:55.166 --> 00:00:57.761
Strict Boolean retrieval has membership,

00:00:58.014 --> 00:00:59.565
not almost-membership.

00:01:00.479 --> 00:01:03.074
Now ask for delulu OR unrealistic.

00:01:03.249 --> 00:01:06.128
Delulu reaches D one and D four.

00:01:06.303 --> 00:01:08.512
Unrealistic reaches D three.

00:01:08.687 --> 00:01:12.056
OR combines the sets, so D one, D three

00:01:12.076 --> 00:01:13.950
and D four are eligible.

00:01:14.526 --> 00:01:16.970
OR includes records satisfying either

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:19.135
condition, including both.

00:01:19.297 --> 00:01:21.120
Adding an alternative can widen

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:24.109
eligibility. It does not, by itself,

00:01:24.129 --> 00:01:26.068
establish whether the extra records help

00:01:26.088 --> 00:01:27.472
with your information need.

00:01:28.364 --> 00:01:29.979
Try delulu NOT interview.

00:01:30.141 --> 00:01:32.337
Start with D one and D four.

00:01:32.512 --> 00:01:35.598
Interview occurs in D one and D two, so

00:01:35.618 --> 00:01:37.298
subtract the overlap.

00:01:37.461 --> 00:01:38.664
D four remains.

00:01:39.215 --> 00:01:41.548
The rule follows the expressed condition,

00:01:41.736 --> 00:01:42.888
not your intention.

00:01:43.051 --> 00:01:45.299
If an otherwise useful record contains the

00:01:45.319 --> 00:01:48.197
excluded term, it can disappear too.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.453
Boolean matching still needs to be judged

00:01:50.473 --> 00:01:52.257
against the purpose of the search.

00:01:53.169 --> 00:01:56.376
The chapter expands delulu into delulu OR

00:01:56.396 --> 00:01:59.416
unrealistic OR irrational OR foolish.

00:01:59.592 --> 00:02:02.355
Suppose foolish is a poor alternative for

00:02:02.375 --> 00:02:03.450
your particular need.

00:02:03.612 --> 00:02:05.693
Adding it can admit records that contain

00:02:05.713 --> 00:02:07.548
foolish but none of the better

00:02:07.568 --> 00:02:08.669
expressions.

00:02:09.223 --> 00:02:11.678
Our extra record E is invented to

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:13.726
illustrate that possibility.

00:02:13.889 --> 00:02:16.665
Ranking may push a weak match down, but

00:02:16.685 --> 00:02:18.494
Boolean has already admitted it.

00:02:18.644 --> 00:02:22.232
Inspect an LLM's proposed alternatives

00:02:22.252 --> 00:02:25.195
before adding them to a formal strategy.

00:02:26.113 --> 00:02:28.493
The reverse error is harder for ranking to

00:02:28.513 --> 00:02:31.921
repair. Change delulu into delulu AND

00:02:31.941 --> 00:02:33.995
interview. D one passes.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:37.204
D four does not, because it has no indexed

00:02:37.224 --> 00:02:39.072
interview term in this example.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:42.111
If D four is useful for your purpose,

00:02:42.325 --> 00:02:44.895
ranking this eligible set cannot bring it

00:02:44.915 --> 00:02:47.344
back. A new search could change the

00:02:47.364 --> 00:02:49.522
conditions. Reordering the admitted

00:02:49.542 --> 00:02:52.098
records cannot change who was admitted.

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:55.888
Boolean logic alone supplies no graded

00:02:55.908 --> 00:02:58.440
relevance score and no rule for which

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:00.707
eligible record should come first.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:02.912
A separate ranking method can order the

00:03:02.932 --> 00:03:06.108
admitted set. Eligibility and usefulness

00:03:06.128 --> 00:03:07.860
remain different questions.

00:03:08.405 --> 00:03:11.313
And satisfying a condition is not always

00:03:11.333 --> 00:03:13.052
literal string identity.

00:03:13.227 --> 00:03:16.132
Analysis, fields, phrases and other

00:03:16.152 --> 00:03:18.941
database rules shape matching first.

00:03:19.116 --> 00:03:21.119
Chapter Two's next question is what

00:03:21.139 --> 00:03:23.400
happens to your words before the gate ever

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:24.302
sees them.
